<title>JAPAN: Tokuyo City Bank sinks to record low in afternoon.</title>
<headline>Tokuyo City Bank sinks to record low in afternoon.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-12-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Tokuyo City Bank Ltd sank to a record low in heavy Friday afternoon trade.</p>
<p>As of 0439 GMT, the shares were down 37 yen at 125 yen, the largest percentage loser on the first section of the Tokyo Stock Exchange. Volume totalled 2.82 million shares, making it the fifth most heavily traded issue.</p>
<p>The previous low was set on November 27 when the issue fell to 155 yen.</p>
